https://github.com/sol4k/sol4k
Reference commit: a166edd854a7198553fdafe9a5051a400d70b121
Copyright sol4k contributors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Little of that code survives unchanged. The module has since been rebuilt
around its own transaction model and request builder, adds v0 address lookup
table selection and v1 (SIMD-0385) transactions, reports every construction
and decoding failure as a typed value rather than an exception, decodes the
wire format without throwing, and reconstructs a compiled transaction back
into an editable request. It targets JVM, Android, macOS and iOS, replaces the
RPC transport, and adds Solana WebSocket subscriptions. Attribution remains
because the work is derived from sol4k, which does not depend on how much of
the original text is still recognisable.

Test fixtures adapted from sol4k at that commit are still carried verbatim,
in src/commonTest/kotlin/io/ethers/solana/UpstreamFixtures.kt.

JVM and Android signing uses org.sol4k:tweetnacl:0.1.6, a current runtime
dependency, separately licensed under the MIT License:
https://github.com/sol4k/tweetnacl
